### Goal Model Design

The goal model is structured to capture the mission requirements for multi-robot resource collection and delivery, considering battery management and failure handling.

#### Goals Table

| Goal ID | Goal Title                  | Text                                                                                     | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type    | Relation | Justification                                                                 |
|--------|-----------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------|-------------|----------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| G1     | Fulfill Resource Request     | Ensure resources are collected from storage and delivered to the specified location.   | -                 | Achieve     | -        | This is the top-level goal ensuring the mission's success condition is met. |
| G2     | Collect Resources            | Gather required resources from storage locations.                                      | -                 | Perform      | G1       | Essential for delivery; must be completed before delivery can begin.      |
| G3     | Deliver Resources             | Transfer collected resources to the specified location.                                 | -                 | Perform      | G1       | Required after collection to fulfill the request.                         |
| G4     | Navigate to Storage           | Move to the storage location where resources are stored.                               | -                 | Perform      | G2       | Navigation is necessary before resource collection.                       |
| G5     | Manage Battery During Collection | Ensure battery level remains above 10% during collection.                          | -                 | Achieve      | G2       | Prevents mission failure due to low battery.                              |
| G6     | Request Resources             | Communicate with storage to retrieve specific resources.                               | -                 | Perform      | G2       | Must occur after navigation to storage.                                     |
| G7     | Navigate to Delivery Location | Travel to the destination for resource delivery.                                         | -                 | Perform      | G3       | Required before delivering resources.                                       |
| G8     | Manage Battery During Delivery | Maintain battery level above 30% during delivery.                                      | -                 | Achieve      | G3       | Ensures mission completion despite battery constraints.                   |
| G9     | Handle Resource Return Failure | Address failure in returning resources to a checkpoint.                                | -                 | Perform      | G8       | Fallback action if resource return fails, ensuring mission integrity.    |

#### Tasks Table

| Task ID | Task Title                     | Text                                                                                     | Relation | Location                | Number of Robots | Justification                                                                 |
|---------|-------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|-------------------------|------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| AT1     | Navigate to Storage             | Move robot to the storage area.                                                         | AND      | Storage Area            | 1                | Single robot needed for navigation.                                           |
| AT2     | Request Specific Resources       | Send request to storage for required resources.                                       | AND      | Storage Area            | 1                | Ensures correct resources are retrieved.                                      |
| AT3     | Transport Resources to Destination | Move resources to the delivery location.                                               | AND      | Delivery Location        | 1                | Single robot handles delivery after collection.                               |
| AT4     | Return Resources to Checkpoint   | Bring resources back to a checkpoint if battery is low.                              | AND      | Checkpoint              | 1                | Ensures resources are secure if delivery is interrupted.                     |
| AT5     | Trigger Resource Alert            | Send alert and report failure to the sector manager.                                 | AND      | Sector Manager's Office | 1                | Mandatory fallback action for mission integrity.                              |

### Summary

- **G1 (Fulfill Resource Request)**: The root goal ensuring all resources are collected and delivered.
- **G2 & G3**: AND decomposition under G1, both essential phases of the mission.
- **G4, G5, G6**: AND under G2, each step crucial for successful collection.
- **G7, G8, G9**: AND under G3, ensuring delivery despite battery constraints and failure handling.

This model ensures structured, efficient mission execution with clear fallback mechanisms for robust performance.
